# Force LF line endings on checkout for source and text files, regardless
# of the checking-out platform's core.autocrlf setting. Windows CI checks
# out with autocrlf true by default, which rewrites LF to CRLF; several
# byte-exact golden/hash comparisons and gofmt (which flags CRLF as
# unformatted) then fail on Windows for a reason that has nothing to do
# with the code under test. See WINDOWS-PARITY-TRIAGE.md category C.
* text=auto eol=lf

# testdata/ subtrees are fixture bytes, not source: fuzz corpus seeds,
# golden hashes, and deliberately-encoded (including CRLF) test inputs.
# These must reach every platform byte-identical to what is committed, so
# they are marked -text to opt them OUT of the line-ending normalization
# above, not to reintroduce it selectively.
**/testdata/** -text
